Z||000000||Richard Parnell||11-12-1999||05:32 PM||||Are there any things I have to be careful of when removing the front and rear fascia on my 87 SC?  Tabs or screws that break, etc?||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||11-12-1999||11:00 PM||||the clip nuts that hold the skirt on the front facia are a pain. Fortunatly you don't have to remove all of them as far as I can tell. only ones that hold the air "duct" pannel in the middle.<P>where you are likely to break some thing ic in the rear trim moulding clips. You want to try to release those from the back side of the pannel if possible. Undo the innner fender first to get more access. ||||reg||1
